NUCRE isolation benchmark — 200 MeV protons in water, NUCRE 3 (inelastic only)
=============================================================================

Part of the issue #212 set (idd_water_200mev_nucre0/1/2/3); see
../idd_water_200mev_nucre0/README for the shared phantom, beam, scoring and the
role of each NUCRE mode.

This case: NUCRE 3 — inelastic nuclear reactions only (Tripathi absorption +
abrasion / compound / Fermi break-up fragmentation), no elastic channel.
OSH-only diagnostic (SH12A has no NUCRE 3), so there is no SH12A mirror deck and
tools/plot_nucre.py shows this mode as OpenShieldHIT-only.  This is where the
secondary alphas, heavy recoils and secondary protons come from today.  Together
with nucre2 this decomposes NUCRE 1.
